/*
audioxt.lcb - xTalk Builder (LCB) binding library for miniaudio, via the
              audio_shim C shim. Part of audioxt for OpenXTalk (OXT).

Once this extension is loaded, every public handler below is callable
directly from xTalk script, e.g.
    put auEngineCreate(0, 0, 0) into sEngine

Nothing here touches the engine's own `play` command or its sound and
player objects: this is a second, separate way to make sound, and a stack
that never calls an au* handler behaves exactly as it did.

Conventions (the shim, src/audio_shim.c, is where each is enforced):
  * Handles are integers (0 = invalid). Every handler tolerates a stale or 0
    handle: getters return 0 or empty, actions do nothing.
  * NAMES ARE MECHANICAL: the handler for the shim's aux_sound_set_volume is
    auSoundSetVolume; nothing is renamed by hand. tools/check-lcb-signatures.py
    holds the bijection (every export bound once, every binding wrapped by the
    one public handler of that name).
  * Every time is in SECONDS. A volume is a multiplier (1 = unchanged).
  * A result of several numbers comes back as TEXT, comma-separated, with a
    "." decimal point in every locale: "x,y,z". Text results cross as a
    Pointer that textOf() copies, never as ZStringNative. Text ARGUMENTS
    (a path, a format name) cross as ZStringUTF8, which the engine makes and
    frees around the call.
  * BYTES IN (a sound file, raw samples) are a Data value: the handler hands
    the shim a pointer and a length, and the shim copies what it keeps
    before it returns. BYTES OUT (decoded or rendered samples, a WAV file,
    what the microphone heard) stay in one buffer the shim owns: the foreign
    call returns the byte count and dataOf() copies that many out at once.
  * A yes/no crosses the public boundary as a Boolean and the C boundary as
    an int (asInt() below; `tR is not 0` on the way back).
  * Nothing here throws, bar the ABI check: a refused call returns 0 or empty
    and auLastError() says why. A sound call on a timer must not be able to
    stop the timer.
  * NOTHING CALLS SCRIPT. The audio system runs on its own threads; they set
    flags, and auPollEnded() reads them on the script's own thread.

The foreign handlers bind to the shared library "audioxt" (built by
CMakeLists.txt). Bindings resolve on first use, so the library only needs to
be present at run time.
*/

/**
Sound for xTalk: many sounds mixed at once with low delay, music streamed
from disk, tones, a microphone, and the samples themselves, through
miniaudio.

An engine (<auEngineCreate>) is a mixer playing into one sound device. A
sound is loaded into an engine from a WAV, FLAC or MP3 file
(<auSoundLoad>), from the bytes of such a file (<auSoundLoadData>), from raw
samples (<auSoundFromPCM>) or made as a tone (<auSoundTone>), and played
with <auSoundStart>. Any number of sounds play at the same time, each with
its own volume, pan and pitch; <auSoundClone> plays one loaded effect many
times at once. Groups (<auGroupCreate>) give several sounds one volume
slider. A sound can also be given a place in 3D (<auSoundSetSpatial>).

A microphone is opened with <auCaptureOpen>; what it hears is read as
samples (<auCaptureRead>) or written straight to a WAV file
(<auCaptureRecordStart>). <auDecodeFile> turns a sound file into samples and
<auWAVEncode> turns samples into a WAV file.

Engines, sounds, groups and captures are integer handles. 0 means a call was
refused, and a stale handle is harmless: getters return 0 or empty, actions
do nothing. <auLastError> says why a call was refused. Every time is in
seconds. The library never sends a message: to learn that a sound has
ended, call <auPollEnded> on a timer. Call <auShutDown> when the stack closes.

This library is separate from the play command and the player object,
which work as they always have.

Tags: Audio, Sound, Library
*/
library org.openxtalk.library.audioxt

use com.livecode.foreign

-- The engine's own builders and readers, resolved by NAME (so no leading
-- underscore): see textOf(), dataOf() and the Data parameters below.
foreign handler MCStringCreateWithBytes(in pBytes as Pointer, in pByteCount as CUInt, in pEncoding as CUInt, in pIsExternalRep as CBool, out rString as String) returns CBool binds to "<builtin>"
foreign handler MCDataCreateWithBytes(in pBytes as Pointer, in pCount as CUInt, out rData as Data) returns CBool binds to "<builtin>"
foreign handler MCDataGetBytePtr(in pData as Data) returns Pointer binds to "<builtin>"

metadata title is "Audio for OpenXTalk"
metadata author is "Seth Morrow Software"
metadata version is "0.1.1"
metadata summary is "Mixing, streaming, tones, 3D sound and microphone capture for xTalk via miniaudio (WAV, FLAC, MP3)."

